# MaCSad public principles and footer

The closing components explain the publication posture and identify the baseline.

## Component PublicPrinciples:
    View:
        css ".principles { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit,minmax(220px,1fr)); gap: 12px; margin-top: 50px; } .principle { padding: 19px; border-top: 2px solid #163e4d; background: rgba(255,255,255,.42); } .principle strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 8px; color: #173642; font-size: 13px; } .principle p { margin: 0; color: #6d787e; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6; }"
        div [class="principles"]:
            div [class="principle"]:
                strong: "Repository grounded"
                p: "Every campaign operates on an immutable snapshot of a watched GitHub workspace."
            div [class="principle"]:
                strong: "Process controlled"
                p: "Roles and decisions move through explicit, inspectable control-flow states."
            div [class="principle"]:
                strong: "Fail closed"
                p: "Missing evidence or approval means a record is not eligible for publication."
            div [class="principle"]:
                strong: "Batch separated"
                p: "The public site is generated from a sealed export, away from private operations."

## Component PublicFooter:
    View:
        css ".footer { padding: 28px clamp(22px,5vw,72px); color: #8da0a8; background: #0c2632; font-size: 11px; } .footer-inner { max-width: 1240px; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 20px; margin: auto; } @media (max-width: 820px) { .footer-inner { flex-direction: column; } }"
        footer [class="footer"]:
            div [class="footer-inner"]:
                span: "MaCSad · Brahmastra Labs"
                span: "Baseline template · no production data"
